swaydesk (0.1.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.1.5.
  * fcitx5 as the session's input method behind a new [enabled]
    input_method key (off by default), so ç and the accents work in
    Chromium and Electron apps; /etc/swaydesk/config.toml is a new
    system layer for [enabled] defaults, which the install images use
    to turn it on.
  * The lock no longer uses swaylock: Swaydesk's own lock first (on
    Debian 13 the GTK 3 one, now in swaydesk-session), gtklock as the
    last resort (a dependency), another lock taking over if one stops,
    and a critical notification if none starts.
  * The lock has its own PAM service, /etc/pam.d/swaydesk-lock; its
    password field never goes through an input method; a refused try
    shows the full PAM message, and the wait after three misses counts
    down.
  * Fixed: dragging a pinned icon in the dock follows the pointer.

 -- Nielson Rolim <nielsonrolim@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:36:47 -0300

swaydesk (0.1.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.1.4.
  * The accent color reaches GTK 3 and GTK 4 apps through gtk.css (only
    when no other desktop is installed), and swaydesk-desktop brings
    adw-gtk-theme (Debian, Ubuntu). New accounts get adw-gtk3-dark when
    Mint-Y is missing; with snapd-desktop-integration (Ubuntu Desktop),
    Adwaita-dark, as in 0.1.3.1. Existing accounts keep their theme.
  * Apps in ~/.config/autostart and /etc/xdg/autostart start in the
    session through systemd and close at logout; what Swaydesk already
    runs (blueman, nm-applet, polkit agents, im-launch, update-notifier,
    touchegg) is skipped. autostart = false in [enabled] turns it off.
  * The settings folders are now called swaydesk (~/.config,
    ~/.local/share, ~/.local/state), moved at the first login with the
    old names left as links; when both exist, the old one stays in use
    and sway.log says so.
  * Power profiles in the System popup on computers without a battery;
    SwayFX 0.6 window animations (animation_duration_ms in [effects]).
  * Arch: swaydesk-desktop depends on paku (>= 0.3.0), and the update
    window runs paku maintain.
  * Login screen and lock: the layout name and the date follow the system
    language and LC_TIME; the login screen logs to the journal
    (journalctl -t swaydesk-greeter), never names or passwords.
  * Ubuntu: a one-time notice with the language-pack command; minimized
    systems keep Swaydesk's translations (swaydesk-dpkg-includes).
  * A new account's 50-local.conf comes in the session's language.
  * Window borders are 3 px; the lock's password field and rofi's search
    take the components' entry style.
  * Fixed: the dock under SwayFX 0.6; the app grid or Super broken by
    another user's session; blueman asking for the admin password at
    login (Debian, Ubuntu); Desktop Theme losing outside changes; no boot
    under Secure Boot after losing the boot entry (swaydesk-efi).

 -- Nielson Rolim <nielsonrolim@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:58:14 -0300

swaydesk (0.1.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Patch release of 0.1.3.
  * With the US international keyboard, ' + c gives c-cedilla (and ' + C
    the capital one) in the session and at the login screen: the session
    creates ~/.XCompose with include "%L", and never touches one of your
    own.
  * A system keyboard change (localectl, dpkg-reconfigure
    keyboard-configuration) reaches existing accounts at their next login,
    unless their keyboard block in 50-local.conf was edited; the login
    screen and new accounts follow it too. On Arch, a stale
    /etc/default/keyboard left by the 0.1.3 installer no longer wins.
  * Dead-key accents work again in GTK 4 apps on Sway without an input
    method (GTK_IM_MODULE=simple when no ibus or fcitx is set up).
  * ~/.local/bin is in the session's PATH on every distro and is created
    at login; the PATH stays out of systemd and D-Bus.

 -- Nielson Rolim <nielsonrolim@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:00:00 -0300

swaydesk (0.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The accent color follows the wallpaper (accent_auto, on by default when
    the accent is still the default one).
  * The icon theme can be chosen: swaydesk-theme icons and the Desktop
    Theme app's Icons list; a theme or color change keeps it.
  * Spanish translation of the desktop, the apps and the login screen.
  * Packages for Debian testing (Debian_Testing), a rolling release tested
    at every release.
  * Arch: an update notice for pacman, the AUR, Flatpak and firmware.
  * swaydesk-sessionmgr asks before restarting or shutting down, with a
    60-second countdown; a pending offline update from GNOME Software 50+
    restarts, installs and powers off on shutdown.
  * swaydesk-greeter ships its own PAM service on Debian and Ubuntu too
    (/etc/pam.d/swaydesk-greeter, Debian 13's greetd file): Debian
    testing's greetd dropped "@include login", and the session lost LANG
    and the keyring unlock.
  * Fixes: the portal after a quick logout and login, the Help icons with
    any icon theme, a missing wallpaper, the default accent swatch, the
    other desktop's portal theme, swaydesk-theme into a closed pipe, the
    theme hints naming swaydesk-theme with the packages, and the Arch gtk
    portal drop-in.

 -- Nielson Rolim <nielsonrolim@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300

swaydesk (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * swaydesk-desktop depends on a polkit agent (mate-polkit | lxpolkit)
    instead of recommending it. On Ubuntu 26.04, network-manager-applet
    depends on "gnome-shell | policykit-1-gnome | polkit-1-auth-agent", and
    apt 3's solver picked gnome-shell: a minimal install pulled the whole
    GNOME desktop and gdm3.
  * Waybar's keyboard layout module is swaydesk-language (custom/language):
    with a single layout it stays hidden after a reload, a theme change or
    a virtual keyboard.
  * swaydesk-common ships Papirus' screen recorder and snapshot icons in
    hicolor (GPL-3), used by Record Screen, Screenshot and the Help cards.
  * The dock hides pins of apps that aren't installed; the first-login
    setup replaces a "nemo" pin with the file manager when Nemo is missing.

